# FASE 10 — Kryon-Qwen3-8B specialist candidate (alternativa a kryon-gpt-oss)
#
# Why this exists: 15 bench runs against THM Pyrat / Operation Endgame
# showed gpt-oss-20b ceils at 2-stage chains under output ambiguity
# (FASES 1-8 documentation). Qwen3-8B Thinking scored notably higher on
# the benchmarks that matter for agentic pentest:
#   - Tau2-Bench (multi-turn tool use): Qwen3.5-4B 79.9 vs gpt-oss-120b 67.8
#   - BFCL-v3 (function calling):       Qwen3 71.9 vs gpt-oss ~67-68
#   - GPQA Diamond (reasoning):         Qwen3 ~78 vs gpt-oss-20b ~71.5
# Trade-off: gpt-oss-20b wins AIME math (98.7 vs ~92) and has 131K
# context vs Qwen3's 33K — neither matters for our use case.
#
# Apache 2.0, ~5 GB VRAM at q4 (vs 11 GB for kryon-gpt-oss) — leaves
# 6+ GB free for parallel training/embedding/etc.

FROM qwen3:8b

# Match the kryon-gpt-oss parameter discipline so the comparison is fair.
# num_ctx 16384 = 5× the working-set ceiling observed in F170 Juice Shop
# bench (~1.3K tokens). Frees memory for KV cache + embeddings.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER num_predict 4096

# Temperature 0.3 — same rationale as kryon-gpt-oss (F179): agentic
# pentest needs reproducible findings, 0.3 keeps variance low while
# leaving enough diversity for alt-path exploration when a tool fails.
# Qwen3 thinking-mode default is 0.6; we override to match gpt-oss
# calibration so bench results are comparable.
PARAMETER temperature 0.3

# Qwen3-recommended sampling for thinking-mode reliability:
# top_p 0.95, top_k 20, min_p 0 (from Qwen3 model card).
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0

# Qwen3 reasoning ON by default — thinking traces emit <think></think>
# tags that the SDK's reasoning parser picks up just like Harmony
# channels (validated F162 path works for both).
# To disable thinking for a specific call use ``/no_think`` in the
# system prompt or ``enable_thinking=False`` via the chat API.

# Stop tokens — Qwen3 native tokens (model card).
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|endoftext|>"
